Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 18:37:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 14/14] v3d: clamp the max LOD of 32-bit-return textures on 3.3

A 32-bit return forces the mip filter to nearest, but a sampler without
mipmapping got a max LOD of 15, so a minified lookup selected levels the
texture doesn't have: wrong data and TMU reads past the BO (MMU errors,
clients 0x2-0xf) in fbo.color with r32f, rg32f and rgba32f cube, 2D array
and 3D textures. Clamp those to the last level.
---
 src/gallium/drivers/v3d/v3dx_emit.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/v3d/v3dx_emit.c b/src/gallium/drivers/v3d/v3dx_emit.c
index 255ee4b..8b4c0ef 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/v3d/v3dx_emit.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/v3d/v3dx_emit.c
@@ -159,12 +159,15 @@ emit_one_texture(struct v3d_context *v3d, struct v3d_texture_stateobj *stage_tex
                                             psview->u.tex.last_level),
                 /* Without mipmapping the filter already selects the base
                  * level. Keep positive LODs so minification can still select
-                 * the min filter on a single-level texture.
+                 * the min filter on a single-level texture. 32-bit returns
+                 * switch the mip filter to nearest below, so they need the
+                 * clamp to the last level.
                  */
                 .max_level_of_detail = MIN2(psview->u.tex.first_level +
                                             MAX2(psampler->max_lod,
                                                  psampler->min_lod),
-                                            psampler->min_mip_filter == PIPE_TEX_MIPFILTER_NONE ?
+                                            psampler->min_mip_filter == PIPE_TEX_MIPFILTER_NONE &&
+                                            return_size != 32 ?
                                             15 : psview->u.tex.last_level),
 
                 .texture_base_pointer = cl_address(rsc->bo,
